From 5401e945ec7a3be47b9479de6cab57e7aa5fabd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 11:51:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc/httpd: remove always-compiled AiCloud/WebDAV code (Phase
 1.3)

usb.c: drop the un-gated (commented-#ifdef) webdav block (write_webdav_permissions
#if 0 helpers, start/stop_webdav incl. the webdav_aidisk/webdav_proxy nvram
cross-enable, stop_all_webdav), the always-compiled start/stop_cloudsync
(~450 lines, all callers CLOUDSYNC-gated), and find_webdav_right +
webdav_account_default (dead, always compiled).
services.c: drop the UNGATED enable_webdav notify handler (bounced
upnp/ddns/firewall and called start_webdav with RTCONFIG_WEBDAV off).
firewall.c: drop the two '#if 1 /* def RTCONFIG_WEBDAV */' LOCALSRV DNAT
blocks and the ungated webdav_aidisk SKIPLOG rule (live firewall writers
keyed on webdav nvram).
httpd: unregister get_webdavInfo.asp (web.c mime table; handler lived in the
closed blob and was served with NO authentication - info-leak surface gone).

#ifdef RTCONFIG_WEBDAV/CLOUDSYNC-gated call sites are left in place: they are
compiled out (flags permanently unset) and deleting them would only add
upstream-merge surface. Entware S50aicloud/S50smartsync #else hooks likewise
kept (inert without /opt scripts). All remaining references verified gated;
stop_all_webdav ungated calls resolve to the rc.h static-inline no-op.
---
